# Docker build-context excludes (repo root).
#
# The standalone deployment images (standalone/docker_stage/*.Dockerfile) build
# with the repo root as their context, so this whole tree is otherwise tarred and
# sent to the daemon on every build. Those builds only COPY:
#   backend/                                (backend.Dockerfile, frontend.Dockerfile use frontend/)
#   frontend/
#   standalone/dist/admin_startup_kit.tar   (backend.Dockerfile)
# The nvflare and mysql images COPY nothing (runtime pip install + volume mounts).
#
# Everything below is test/runtime output, a local cache, or a dev artifact that
# no image build depends on.
#
# DO NOT add `dist/` or `build/` here: backend.Dockerfile needs standalone/dist/.

# --- Test & runtime output (the recurring build-context breakers) ---
# The docker simulator-sweep runner writes root-owned (mode 700) simulator-workspaces/
# dirs under test-results/; Docker's context sender cannot read them and the build
# fails with "open ...: permission denied".
**/test-results
standalone/job-results
standalone/nvflare_workspace
**/nvflare_workspace

# --- VCS ---
.git

# --- Python caches / bytecode / packaging metadata ---
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# --- Virtual environments ---
**/.venv
**/venv

# --- Node ---
**/node_modules

# --- Local env / secrets (compose reads .env.local from the host at runtime;
#     it is never needed inside an image layer) ---
**/.env.local
**/*.env.local

# --- Editor / OS junk ---
.vscode
.idea
*.code-workspace
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
